    "summary": "Spec 39 step 9 split (under the user's standing leave to split, recorded in the spec), and its first part built: LoadPaths and StructureSupports port to the crate as they were (`native/rust/src/structure.rs`, `structure/supports.rs`). `solve` gives each element's and ground column's load and what fails, in the order found; `settle` follows the collapse through on a copy. Keys stay GDScript's strings, so every sort is the same, and the plan's keyed lists are read the way GDScript's dictionaries held them (a cell drawn twice is one element, in the place it was first drawn, using its last drawing). `sim/structure/` and its gdUnit tests are gone. Nothing in the game called them.",
